        {
            "src": "2607.25356v1/x5.png",
            "data": "",
            "alt": "Refer to caption",
            "desc": "3.3 E3 — Budget–Accuracy Trade-off\n\n\nTable 8 shows mean relative error of random_uniform and\ndag at each sampling budget on D2, D3, and D4.\n\n\nTable 8: E3 — Mean relative error vs. budget (3 seeds/cell). dag\nis budget-invariant at 19–27%. Bold = lowest RU error per dataset\n(D2 at 5%, C2; D3 and D4 at 50%). The bolded D2/RU value at bb=5%\nis 0.0049 (0.49%, C2), shown rounded to .005.\n\n\n\nDataset\nMethod\n\nbb=5%\n\n\nbb=10%\n\n\nbb=20%\n\n\nbb=30%\n\n\nbb=50%\n\n\n\n\n\nD2 (NYC 311)\nRU\n.005\n.007\n.004\n.003\n.003\n\n\ndag\n.195\n.196\n.196\n.195\n.194\n\n\nD3 (NYPD)\nRU\n.037\n.024\n.020\n.010\n.001\n\n\ndag\n.213\n.213\n.213\n.213\n.213\n\n\nD4 (Adult)\nRU\n.027\n.025\n.021\n.018\n.011\n\n\ndag\n.273\n.274\n.260\n.262\n.264\n\n\n\n\n\nFinding (C2).\nOn D2 (NYC 311, 500K rows), random_uniform reaches 0.49%\nmean relative error at a 5% sampling budget, far below the 1% threshold with\nonly 25K rows inspected.\nstrat-quality matches this on D2 (0.49% at bb=5%); cluster\nreaches 1.42% at bb=5% and converges to 0.21% at bb=50%\n(Table 8 lists RU and dag; per-budget values for all\nnine methods are in the released results).\ndag is insensitive to budget on all three real datasets (19–27%\nregardless of bb), confirming that its proxy mismatch is structural\n(Figure 2).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFigure 1: E1 — Mean relative error per method at bb=50% on all four\nprimary datasets. D1=synthetic 100K; D2=NYC 311 (500K); D3=NYPD\narrests (500K); D4=UCI Adult census (49K). DAG-MCMC is\nworst on all real-world datasets (D2–D4);\nUniform and Cluster are near zero.\n\n\nFigure 2: E3 — Relative error vs. sampling budget bb.\nD2=NYC 311; D3=NYPD arrests; D4=UCI Adult census.\ndag is budget-invariant at ≈\\approx19–27%;\nRU converges to sub-1% at bb=5% on D2.",
